WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.617
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.917 --> 00:00:09.675
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:15.066
Unit seventeen: Reported Questions. Today you will report questions that someone asked.

4
00:00:15.366 --> 00:00:18.111
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:22.241
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.083 --> 00:00:23.933
Asked.

7
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.903
Asked means the past of ask.

8
00:00:27.517 --> 00:00:28.994
She asked where I lived.

9
00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:31.783
Your turn. Say: Asked.

10
00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:35.483
Asked.

11
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:37.321
Wanted to know.

12
00:00:38.317 --> 00:00:40.897
Wanted to know means a way to report a question.

13
00:00:41.483 --> 00:00:43.007
He wanted to know my name.

14
00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:46.141
Your turn. Say: Wanted to know.

15
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.152
Wanted to know.

16
00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:52.011
If/whether.

17
00:00:53.017 --> 00:00:55.806
If/whether means used in reported yes/no questions.

18
00:00:56.417 --> 00:00:57.940
She asked if I was ready.

19
00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:01.400
Your turn. Say: If/whether.

20
00:01:04.233 --> 00:01:05.269
If/whether.

21
00:01:06.017 --> 00:01:07.308
Reported speech.

22
00:01:08.317 --> 00:01:11.175
Reported speech means telling what someone said.

23
00:01:11.783 --> 00:01:13.388
This is reported speech.

24
00:01:13.983 --> 00:01:17.054
Your turn. Say: Reported speech.

25
00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:21.331
Reported speech.

26
00:01:22.083 --> 00:01:23.456
Word order change.

27
00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:27.227
Word order change means moving to statement order.

28
00:01:27.817 --> 00:01:29.456
There is a word order change.

29
00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:32.760
Your turn. Say: Word order change.

30
00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:37.298
Word order change.

31
00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:39.051
Tense shift.

32
00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:43.118
Tense shift means moving the verb one step back.

33
00:01:43.717 --> 00:01:45.380
A tense shift happens.

34
00:01:45.983 --> 00:01:48.369
Your turn. Say: Tense shift.

35
00:01:51.233 --> 00:01:52.234
Tense shift.

36
00:01:52.983 --> 00:01:54.298
Direct question.

37
00:01:55.283 --> 00:01:57.817
Direct question means the exact question.

38
00:01:58.417 --> 00:01:59.557
Where do you live?

39
00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:02.942
Your turn. Say: Direct question.

40
00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:06.975
Direct question.

41
00:02:07.717 --> 00:02:09.089
Indirect question.

42
00:02:10.083 --> 00:02:12.547
Indirect question means the reported form.

43
00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:14.546
She asked where I lived.

44
00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:18.046
Your turn. Say: Indirect question.

45
00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.365
Indirect question.

46
00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:26.608
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:30.599
Visal, tell me a question someone asked you recently.

48
00:02:31.683 --> 00:02:42.628
My teacher asked me, Do you understand? Reported: She asked me if I understood. In reported questions we change the word order and the tense.

49
00:02:43.717 --> 00:02:45.554
What happens to the word order?

50
00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:55.644
It becomes statement order. We say He asked where I lived, not he asked where did I live. There is no do or does and no question mark.

51
00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:58.390
And yes/no questions?

52
00:02:59.483 --> 00:03:11.461
We use if or whether: She asked if I was ready. Time words may change too: tomorrow becomes the next day. The tense shifts back, like in other reported speech.

53
00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.042
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:14.883 --> 00:03:21.074
Grammar focus: Reported questions: asked plus if and question word plus statement order.

55
00:03:21.374 --> 00:03:22.677
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:23.383 --> 00:03:24.860
She asked where I lived.

57
00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:27.390
He asked if I was ready.

58
00:03:28.283 --> 00:03:30.747
They wanted to know what time the shop opened.

59
00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:40.192
Reported questions use statement order, no do / does, no question mark. Use if / whether for yes/no questions, and move the tense back.

60
00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:44.357
Be careful! Don't say: He asked where did I live.

61
00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.265
Say: He asked where I lived.

62
00:03:48.565 --> 00:03:50.100
Use statement order.

63
00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:53.459
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:55.813
Passing On Questions.

65
00:03:56.113 --> 00:03:58.670
My teacher asked me if I understood the lesson.

66
00:03:59.667 --> 00:04:01.306
She wanted to know where I lived.

67
00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.265
He asked what time the shop opened.

68
00:04:05.267 --> 00:04:08.984
In indirect questions, there is a word order change and a tense shift.

69
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.441
The direct question is the exact question.

70
00:04:13.533 --> 00:04:17.814
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:21.732
'Where do you live?' → She asked where I blank.

72
00:04:22.032 --> 00:04:25.198
A, live. B, lived. C, do live.

73
00:04:28.733 --> 00:04:30.779
The answer is B: lived.

74
00:04:31.917 --> 00:04:35.347
'Are you ready?' → He asked blank I was ready.

75
00:04:35.647 --> 00:04:38.580
A, if. B, that. C, what.

76
00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:43.610
The answer is A: if.

77
00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:46.332
Which sentence is correct?

78
00:04:46.632 --> 00:04:52.584
A, He asked where did I go.. B, He asked where I went.. C, He asked where I go did..

79
00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:58.713
The answer is B: He asked where I went..

80
00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:02.035
A reported question has no blank.

81
00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:05.954
A, question mark. B, subject. C, verb.

82
00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.685
The answer is A: question mark.

83
00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:15.871
According to the reading, what did she want to know?

84
00:05:16.171 --> 00:05:19.650
A, where I lived. B, my age. C, my job.

85
00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:25.385
The answer is A: where I lived.

86
00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:29.949
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:30.783 --> 00:05:33.410
Report a question someone recently asked you.

88
00:05:42.217 --> 00:05:43.833
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:55.995
My neighbour asked me where I was going. She also wanted to know if I would come back soon. I use statement order and the past tense in reported questions.

90
00:05:56.295 --> 00:05:57.876
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:58.783 --> 00:06:05.789
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and reported questions: asked plus if and question word plus statement order.

92
00:06:06.089 --> 00:06:10.332
Today's value is communication. Speak clearly and listen carefully.

93
00:06:10.632 --> 00:06:13.366
See you in Unit eighteen. Goodbye!

94
00:06:13.666 --> 00:06:16.794
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

